---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Recall People"
  description="Privacy Policy for Recall People app. Learn how we handle your data."
>
  <main class="min-h-screen page-shell text-foreground">
    <div class="pt-24 pb-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">
            Privacy Policy
          </h1>
          <p class="text-text-secondary mb-8">
            Last updated: July 17, 2026
          </p>

          <div class="prose prose-stone max-w-none">
            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                1. Overview
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Recall People (&quot;we&quot;, &quot;our&quot;, or &quot;the app&quot;) is a privacy-first personal CRM
                that helps you remember the people you meet. We are committed to protecting your privacy
                and being transparent about how we handle your data.
              </p>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                <strong class="text-text-primary">Key principle:</strong> Your relationship data is synced
                through your account so the app can work across devices. Sensitive content, including notes,
                memories, and relationship context, is encrypted in our database. We do not sell your personal
                data or use it to train AI models.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                2. Data We Collect
              </h2>

              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-3 mt-6">
                2.1 Relationship Data Synced Through Your Account
              </h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                The following app content is associated with your account and synced so you can access it
                across your devices:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>Contact information (names, phone numbers, emails, birthdays)</li>
                <li>Notes and memories about your contacts</li>
                <li>Transcriptions of voice recordings (the audio itself is not stored by Recall People after transcription)</li>
                <li>AI-generated summaries and conversation starters</li>
                <li>Groups, tags, and events you create</li>
                <li>Custom avatars generated for contacts</li>
              </ul>

              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-3 mt-6">
                2.2 Account Data
              </h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                We store the minimum data needed to provide authentication, secure sync, preferences,
                and paid features:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2 mb-4">
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Name (if provided)</li>
                <li>Authentication tokens for secure login</li>
                <li>Preferred language, subscription status, and usage counters for plan limits</li>
                <li>Operational security logs such as IP address, user agent, action type, and success or failure status</li>
              </ul>

              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-3 mt-6">
                2.3 Sensitive Data and AI Processing
              </h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                Sensitive relationship content is encrypted in our database. AI features remain disabled until
                you give explicit permission in the app. If you consent and request an AI feature, only the
                relevant content is sent to the provider needed to deliver it:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Voice recordings:</strong> Sent to Groq for transcription using Whisper. We do not store those recordings on our servers.</li>
                <li><strong>Text for AI analysis:</strong> Sent to Cerebras to extract contacts, generate summaries, run semantic search, and answer your questions via the Assistant.</li>
                <li><strong>Avatar generation:</strong> Text descriptions such as gender, age range, and style are sent to OpenAI GPT Image 2 to generate illustrated contact avatars. No real photos are required for this feature.</li>
                <li><strong>Quality evaluation:</strong> If server-side quality evaluation is enabled, a sampled subset of AI inputs and responses may be sent to xAI Grok to assess result quality.</li>
              </ul>

              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-3 mt-6">
                2.4 Product Analytics, Reliability, and AI Observability
              </h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                Recall People uses PostHog Cloud EU on the public website, in the mobile app, and on the backend
                to understand feature usage, diagnose errors, secure the service, and monitor AI cost and reliability.
                Depending on the surface, PostHog receives an internal user identifier, authentication provider type,
                product-interaction events, counters and booleans, device or technical context, and error diagnostics.
              </p>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                We do not send contact names, note text, transcriptions, search queries, or relationship content in
                product analytics events. Click/touch autocapture, session replay, and IP-derived location enrichment
                are disabled on both the website and mobile app. AI prompts
                and outputs are redacted from automated AI observability; manual transcription and avatar telemetry
                contains operational metadata such as model, latency, duration, byte count, or output length, not content.
                We do not use PostHog for advertising or cross-app tracking.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                3. How We Use Your Data
              </h2>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li>Transcribe your voice recordings into text</li>
                <li>Extract contact information and events from your notes</li>
                <li>Generate AI summaries and conversation starters</li>
                <li>Create custom avatars for your contacts</li>
                <li>Answer your questions about your contacts via the Assistant</li>
                <li>Send you notifications about upcoming events (if enabled)</li>
                <li>Sync relationship data through your account</li>
                <li>Manage your account and subscription</li>
                <li>Protect the service, prevent abuse, and debug reliability issues</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                4. Third-Party Services
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
                We use the following third-party services to provide app functionality:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Groq:</strong> Speech-to-text transcription using Whisper</li>
                <li><strong>Cerebras:</strong> AI analysis, contact extraction, summaries, and AI assistant</li>
                <li><strong>OpenAI GPT Image 2:</strong> AI avatar generation from text descriptions</li>
                <li><strong>xAI Grok:</strong> Sampled AI response quality evaluation when enabled</li>
                <li><strong>RevenueCat:</strong> Subscription and payment management via App Store / Google Play</li>
                <li><strong>Google Sign-In / Apple Sign-In:</strong> Optional authentication methods</li>
                <li><strong>PostHog Cloud EU:</strong> Product analytics, error diagnostics, service reliability, and redacted AI operational telemetry</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-4">
                These services process data only as needed to provide their functionality and are bound by
                their own privacy policies and data processing terms.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                5. Data Storage and Security
              </h2>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li>Relationship data is synced through your account</li>
                <li>Sensitive content, including notes, memories, and relationship context, is encrypted in our database</li>
                <li>Authentication tokens are stored securely using your device&apos;s keychain (iOS) or keystore (Android)</li>
                <li>All communications with our servers use HTTPS encryption</li>
                <li>We limit internal access to personal data to what is needed to operate, secure, and support the service</li>
                <li>We do not sell your personal data</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                6. AI and Your Data
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-4">
                <strong class="text-text-primary">Your data is never used to train AI models.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                Before any AI feature shares personal data with Groq, Cerebras, OpenAI, or xAI, the app explains
                what is processed, names the providers, and asks for your permission. You can decline and
                continue using non-AI features. If you later request an AI feature, the app asks again.
                Once enabled, your data is sent only when you request AI processing. We configure these
                services so your inputs and outputs are not used for model training, except where you separately
                choose to share data with a provider outside Recall People.
              </p>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                Providers may retain limited operational, safety, abuse-prevention, billing, or usage
                metrics under their own terms. Cerebras states that it does not retain inference inputs and
                outputs. Groq does not retain inference content by default, but may keep it temporarily for
                reliability or abuse review. xAI states that API requests and responses are retained for up to
                30 days unless Zero Data Retention applies. OpenAI may retain API inputs and outputs for a
                limited period for safety, abuse prevention, and service operation according to its API data controls.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                7. Your Rights
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-3">
                You have full control over your data:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Access:</strong> View all your data directly in the app</li>
                <li><strong>Export:</strong> Export your data anytime in JSON or CSV format</li>
                <li><strong>Delete:</strong> Delete individual contacts, notes, or your entire account</li>
                <li><strong>AI choice:</strong> Decline third-party AI processing, continue using non-AI features, or change your choice under Profile → Data → AI data processing</li>
                <li><strong>Portability:</strong> Your exported data can be used elsewhere</li>
                <li><strong>Correction:</strong> Edit your contact and note data directly in the app</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                8. Data Retention
              </h2>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-text-secondary space-y-2">
                <li>Relationship data remains associated with your account until you delete it or request account deletion</li>
                <li>Deleting the app from one device does not automatically delete synced account data</li>
                <li>Account data is retained until you request deletion or as otherwise required for legal, billing, security, or abuse-prevention reasons</li>
                <li>Operational logs are retained only as long as needed for security, debugging, abuse prevention, and legal obligations</li>
                <li>Analytics and reliability events are retained according to our PostHog configuration and deleted or anonymized when no longer needed for those purposes</li>
                <li>Voice recordings sent for transcription are not stored by Recall People after processing</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mt-4">
                You can delete your account inside the app. For accounts linked to Sign in with Apple, Recall People
                asks you to reauthenticate and revokes the Apple authorization before deleting the account. Deleting
                your Recall People account does not cancel an App Store or Google Play subscription; subscriptions
                must be managed through the relevant store.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                9. International Transfers
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                Our service providers may process data in countries outside your country of residence,
                including the United States. When this happens, processing is governed by the provider&apos;s
                contractual and legal safeguards.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                10. Legal Basis
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                Where applicable privacy laws require a legal basis, we process data to provide the app
                and your account, with your consent for AI processing, to comply with legal obligations,
                and for our legitimate interests in security, abuse prevention, debugging, and improving
                service reliability.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                11. Children&apos;s Privacy
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                Recall People is not intended for children under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly
                collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe we have collected
                such information, please contact us immediately.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                12. Changes to This Policy
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                We may update this privacy policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes
                by posting the new policy on this page and updating the &quot;Last updated&quot; date.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">
                13. Contact Us
              </h2>
              <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
                If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, our data practices, or a request to
                access, correct, export, or delete account data, please contact us at:
              </p>
              <p class="text-text-secondary mt-3">
                <a href="mailto:privacy@recallpeople.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">
                  privacy@recallpeople.com
                </a>
              </p>
            </section>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border-light">
            <a
              href="/"
              class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-white hover:bg-primary text-text-primary hover:text-white font-semibold rounded-xl border-2 border-border transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
            >
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"></path>
              </svg>
              Back to Home
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>
